      "id": 1,
      "text": "Jordan’s 1830s boom featured three gristmills, three sawmills, a sash factory, a distillery, a clothing shop, five taverns, seven general stores, two drug stores, and five grocery stores.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://jordanny.gov/history-overview",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Jordan Hotel, originally the Clinton House, opened in 1820 as a modest two‑story building.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://jordanny.gov/history-overview",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Local lore says Jordan got its name from a story told by Bessie Sharp in 1938.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://jordanny.gov/history-overview",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "vague"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Erie Canal turned Jordan into a commercial, industrial, and transportation center during the 1830s‑1840s and again in the 1870s‑1880s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://jordanny.gov/history-overview",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Early twentieth‑century Jordan enjoyed both railroad and trolley service, linking it to larger markets.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://jordanny.gov/history-overview",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Every summer, Jordan hosts the Skaneateles Festival of Music, an Antique Boat Show, and Dickens Christmas with actors in period costume.",
